{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, Mr. Whittaker. I'm Megan Kowalczyk, the nurse practitioner in the Heart Failure Clinic.",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 8.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Darnell Whittaker, February 27, 1958.",
   "start": 14.7,
   "end": 18.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thank you. The nurse said you called on Monday about some swelling. What's been happening?",
   "start": 19.42,
   "end": 26.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, my ankles have been puffing up for about a week. My shoes are tight by the afternoon and the scale says I'm up seven pounds.",
   "start": 27.5,
   "end": 34.62
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, what's your usual weight at home?",
   "start": 34.62,
   "end": 38.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm usually right around 182. This morning it was 189.",
   "start": 38.84,
   "end": 43.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And how's your breathing? Worse than usual,",
   "start": 44.7,
   "end": 47.48
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "normally I can walk three blocks to the corner store. Now I'm winded after about one block.",
   "start": 47.78,
   "end": 52.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How many pillows are you sleeping on?",
   "start": 53.46,
   "end": 55.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I've gone from one pillow to two. Feels easier to breathe propped up.",
   "start": 56.39,
   "end": 60.15
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Are you waking up at night, gasping for air? No, not that. Any chest pain, or feeling like you might pass out.",
   "start": 60.65,
   "end": 70.38
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No chest pain, no passing out.",
   "start": 71.06,
   "end": 72.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Anything different with your diet the last couple of years. Well my nephew got married two weekends ago.",
   "start": 73.72,
   "end": 80.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "There was a lot of ham, a lot of salty food. I wasn't careful, I'll admit it. My wife Lorraine already gave me an earful.",
   "start": 81.25,
   "end": 88.11
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That happens, let's go through your medicines. You're on Sacubitril Valsartan, 49 and 51 milligrams twice a day. Carvedilol, 12 .5 milligrams twice a day. Spironolactone, 25 milligrams once a day. Piglifflesin, 10 milligrams once a day. Still taking all of though.",
   "start": 88.57,
   "end": 115.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Every one of them, Lorraine fills my pill box on Sundays.",
   "start": 117.06,
   "end": 120.14
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And the Furosemide, how much are you taking?",
   "start": 120.66,
   "end": 123.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "The water pill is 20 milligrams in the morning. weight no it's the 40 they changed it in the summer it's 40",
   "start": 124.52,
   "end": 131.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "yes 40 milligrams once a day is what I have anything",
   "start": 131.56,
   "end": 137.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "um I've been taking naproxen for my knees the arthritis acts up two of the 220 milligram pills twice a day for about",
   "start": 139.06,
   "end": 147.88
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "two weeks okay that's important let me check you over your weight here is 189 blood pressure is 112 over 70, pulse 78 oxygen is 95 % on room air, your neck veins I hear some crackles at the bottom of both lungs, heart is regular and I hear a soft extra sound S3 got 2 plus pitting swelling up to the middle of both shins.",
   "start": 147.88,
   "end": 193.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That doesn't sound great.",
   "start": 193.96,
   "end": 195.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "It tells me you're holding onto extra fluid. Your last echo showed an ejection fraction of 30%. So your heart pump is weaker than enough to salt from three weeks ago or okay.",
   "start": 196.08,
   "end": 215.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So what do we do?",
   "start": 222.63,
   "end": 223.43
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So this is a mild flare of your heart failure with reduced ejection fraction. I think the salty food needs hold onto salt. I want you to stop it completely.",
   "start": 224.01,
   "end": 245.27
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "What do I take for the knees then?",
   "start": 245.92,
   "end": 247.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "acetaminide is safer for your heart. You can take 650 milligrams up to three times a day. For the fluid, I'm increasing the furosemide to 40 milligrams twice a day. Once your weight is back near 183 to 40 milligrams once a day.",
   "start": 248.26,
   "end": 275.95
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay 40 twice a day for five days.",
   "start": 276.85,
   "end": 278.71
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "All your other heart medicine. Weigh yourself every morning after you use the bathroom. Two thousand milligrams a day and fluids out two liters.",
   "start": 280.4,
   "end": 297.74
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Lorraine's going to love that. She's been on me about the salt.",
   "start": 298.47,
   "end": 301.37
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'd also like a basic metabolic pad 21st of October. Make sure your kidneys and up three pounds get chest pain.",
   "start": 302.39,
   "end": 327.64
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Got it.",
   "start": 330.98,
   "end": 331.48
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And are you using the patient portal? Send you the instructions there.",
   "start": 331.98,
   "end": 337.58
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, it's darnell .widacre at examplymail .com.",
   "start": 338.22,
   "end": 341.74
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'll send the plan there. I want to see you back in a week to check your way. Sounds good.",
   "start": 344.01,
   "end": 351.81
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thank you, Megan.",
   "start": 352.11,
   "end": 352.61
  }
 ],
